{"ts":"2026-09-25T21:20:03.592Z","author":"agent.claude.test-pilot","name":"messages/assistant/00000006","body":"Steps 1–6 are done. The child (`child-1`, haiku) was still running at the last poll, so I'm ending the turn without waiting for it. I ran no extra tests.\n\n**Onboarding**\n- I listed `origins/` (24 entries) and read `origins/onboarding_1.12.md` in one `fs_read` call. It returned all 262 lines with `next_line` null. [checked]\n- Substantive tools worked afterwards. That is consistent with the gate having opened, but I didn't test the gate itself. [working]\n\n**Step 1 – draft and export**\n- `pilot/draft` was written with body `print('draft')` and tag `pilot.note`. Its ID is `20260925T211931Z:86`. [checked]\n- `fs_write` exported that body to `workspace/chat-20260925t211931z-e36e4a0e79/smoke-draft.py`, 14 bytes. [checked]\n\n**Step 2 – safe script**\n- `python_execute` on `scripts:/safe_test.py` finished with exit code 0, status completed, not timed out and not truncated. [checked]\n- The output is stored as `pilot/script-output` (`20260925T211931Z:155`, author `harness`). Its body reads: `safe_test diagnostic: completed {\"script\": \"safe_test\", \"sum\": 42, \"filesystem_writes\": false}`. [checked via `ledger_read`]\n\n**Step 3 – expected refusal**\n- `python_execute` on `workspace:/smoke-draft.py` with output name `pilot/denied-output` was refused with `capability_denied`.\n- The message was \"Outside fs.execute bounds … held: ['scripts:/safe_test.py']\", so it names both the path and the grant. [checked]\n- I did not read `pilot/denied-output`. I don't know whether the harness reserved it despite the refusal. [unchecked]\n\n**Step 4 – instructions**\n- `pilot/instructions` was written as `20260925T211931Z:106`. It includes the Bar line and matches your text. [checked]\n\n**Step 5 – child start**\n- I started `child-1` with model haiku, instructions ID `20260925T211931Z:106`, result name `pilot/child-result`, and exactly the bounds you gave. [checked]\n- You said to grant reads of the instruction note and the result name explicitly. `ledger.read: [\"pilot/**\"]` already covers both, so I did not widen anything.\n- The child can't read `bootstrap-harness/rules.md`, because its `fs.read` is only `origins/**`. That is the refusal its instructions expect.\n\n**Step 6 – while the child runs**\n- `add(20, 22)` returned 42. [checked]\n- `subagent_status` with `wait_seconds` 0 shows `running`, with result null and error null. [checked]\n\n**Not yet known**\n- Whether the child got its `add` call and its `rules.md` refusal, whether it wrote `pilot/child/report`, and what lands in `pilot/child-result`. [unchecked]\n\n**Discrepancies:** none found.\n\n**Ambiguities**\n- The child's onboarding read is a no-op. Its instructions say \"read your required onboarding\" but don't name a file. Its `origins/**` bound allows the read.\n- The child's `fs.read` doesn't cover `bootstrap-harness/rules.md`. Under the harness's path mapping, it may show as a bounds refusal or as a path/mapping error. That will be informative either way."}
