{"ts":"2026-09-25T21:20:32.437Z","author":"agent.claude.test-pilot","name":"messages/assistant/00000012","body":"**Verification summary.** I ran no additional tests. I only read the records.\n\n**Child status** [checked: `subagent_status`]\n- `child-1` reports `completed`, with no error.\n- Its result is `pilot/child-result` (`20260925T211931Z:540`, author `agent.claude.child-1`), tagged `agent.result`, `output.finished`, `output.reserved`.\n\n**Child evidence**\n- **`pilot/child/report`** (`20260925T211931Z:508`, author `agent.claude.child-1`, tag `pilot.note`, prev null):\n  - It says the onboarding file was read in full, lines 1–262 with `next_line` null.\n  - It says `add(19, 23)` gave 42.\n  - It says `fs_read` on `bootstrap-harness/rules.md` gave `capability_denied`, and that the child's `fs.read` was `origins/**`.\n- **`pilot/child-result`** matches that report. Its body is a running narration plus a summary, and it cites report ID `:508`, which matches the actual ledger ID.\n- The child's account of the refusal looks consistent with my own `capability_denied` result in step 3. I can't independently confirm the child's tool calls, because I can't see its transcript. I'm relying on its own account, plus the fact that the report exists with the expected author and tag. [working]\n\n**Parent evidence** [checked: `ledger_read` this turn, and the earlier turn]\n- `pilot/script-output` (`:155`, author `harness`) reads `safe_test diagnostic: completed {\"script\": \"safe_test\", \"sum\": 42, \"filesystem_writes\": false}`.\n- The exit code 0 came from the `python_execute` return in the earlier turn.\n- `add(20, 22)` gave 42. The child's `add(19, 23)` also gave 42.\n\n**Discrepancies**\n- No `DISCREPANCY:` items in the strict sense. The child's report matches its instructions, and the ledger IDs match.\n- Observations that may matter:\n  1. The child's result body includes narration that isn't a \"short report\", such as \"Let me start by listing…\". That is a mild deviation from \"return a short report\". It is probably just the haiku model's output, and the record is intact.\n  2. The child report says \"Ready to receive directed work\" and claims \"All … completed successfully\". That is self-assessment and not independently verified.\n  3. Ambiguity from my earlier note: the child instructions didn't name an onboarding file. The child chose `origins/onboarding_1.12.md`, and I didn't check how it chose it beyond its own listing and reading.\n- **Unchecked:** I never read `pilot/denied-output`, so I don't know whether the harness reserved it after the refusal. You didn't ask for that read, and I ran no further tests.\n\n**Overall:** all six directed steps have surviving records, and the expected refusals (mine and the child's) both happened."}
